X:4
T:Click Go The Shears
M:4/4
N:I don't know much about this one. We needed something for a Canadian barn-dance, and this is what came into Simon's head. We may have folk-processed it somewhat ...
N:He thought it might be Australian, but other sources on the 'net seem to credit it to Henry Clay Work, USA
O:Australia
R:Barndance
Z:Richard Robinson <URL:http://www.qualmograph.org.uk/contact.html>
K:D major
F2 F>E D2 F>A | d2 d>c B4     | A2  A>B A>F D>E | F2 E2 E4 |
F2 F>E D2 F>A | d2 d>c B2 c>d | e>d c>B A>G F>E | D2 d2 d4 ||
e2 e>d c>d e2 | d2  f>d A4     | B2  B>c d>c d>B | A>B A>F E2 D>E |
F2 F>E D2 F>A | d>e d>c B2 c>d | e>d c>B A>G F>E | D2 d2 d4|]
% Source: sources/richardrobinson-tunebook-org-uk/data/tunebook.abc

X:5
T:Click Go The Shears
M:4/4
N:I don't know much about this one. We needed something for a Canadian barn-dance, and this is what came into Simon's head. We may have folk-processed it somewhat ...
N:He thought it might be Australian, but other sources on the 'net seem to credit it to Henry Clay Work, USA
O:Australia
R:Barndance
Z:Richard Robinson <URL:http://www.qualmograph.org.uk/contact.html>
